WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:04.917
I just wanna dance with you

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.625
Let the whole world
melt away

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:10.958
And dance with you

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:13.750
Who cares
what other people say

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:17.042
And when we're through

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:23.167
No one can convince us
we were wrong

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.500
All it takes is you and me

00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:31.583
And a song

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:41.917
Gotta close your eyes.
Close your eyes.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.000
It takes a few seconds.

00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:48.417
Oh my goodness!

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:50.625
Open, open, open!

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:56.000
What is it?

00:00:56.792 --> 00:00:58.333
-Dinosaurs.
-Where?

00:00:58.417 --> 00:00:59.958
You don't see
all these dinosaurs?

00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:02.417
Look around.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.000
Look at all these dinosaurs.

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:07.708
You see 'em?

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:08.792
Yeah!

00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:11.000
Hey, come on,
come on, come on.

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:12.500
-Wait, watch out!
-What is it?

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:14.500
Don't step in the fire,
we're cave men.

00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:16.000
We need this fire

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:17.375
'cause there's
no electricity

00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:18.750
and it's cold
out here, okay?

00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:21.625
-Watch out, watch out!
-Oh, my good-- a T-rex!

00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:24.583
That's a T--get your stuff.
Get your stuff. Get, get it!

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.375
We gotta find
some place safe.

00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:31.875
-Like what?
-We need a cave.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.208
A cave?

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.000
We gotta find a cave,
come on.

00:01:35.083 --> 00:01:36.250
-Okay.
-Come on, come on.

00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:39.458
Hey, Vivian. Vivian.
Wait, wait.

00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:43.625
Look, it's fine, okay.
I was just confused.

00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:45.833
You don't have to run
out of your car about it.

00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:46.750
I like you.

00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:49.250
A lot. I do.

00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:51.792
I don't know.
Got all in my head about it

00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:53.375
and then I started worrying

00:01:53.458 --> 00:01:55.542
that maybe I shouldn't
come off too strong.

00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:57.875
You know, you're like this
super powerful feminist

00:01:57.958 --> 00:01:59.375
and not just a cute girl.

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:02.208
I mean, you are a cute girl,
don't get me wrong--

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.000
There it is.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.875
It's my old duffel coat.

00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:20.917
Actually, it was mine first.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.750
Well, long before that
it was mine.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.708
-Oh, was it Mr. Brown?
-Really?

00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:27.250
He wore it
on his first day at school.

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:28.667
It's lovely!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.500
Wooden buttons
for ease of paw,

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.125
these two
sandwich compartments

00:02:33.208 --> 00:02:34.333
are an excellent idea.

00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:36.000
I must say,
it suits you very well.

00:02:36.542 --> 00:02:39.167
I never thought I'd like
a human coat, but...

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.708
You look like
one of the family.

00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:46.167
These hallways are murder.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.292
I'm Ellie Chu.

00:02:50.792 --> 00:02:51.625
Yes, I know.

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:54.625
We've only been playing
my dad's services

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:56.167
every Sunday
for like four years.

00:02:58.208 --> 00:02:59.583
You're his favourite
heathen.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.583
He can't handle
mediocre accompanists.

00:03:02.125 --> 00:03:03.208
Even if they are saved.

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.125
Remains of the Day.

00:03:08.625 --> 00:03:09.542
Loved it.

00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:13.000
All that
barely repressed longing.

00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:24.125
Oh, hi.

00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:25.167
Who is it?

00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:31.583
It's carol singers.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.417
Give them a quid,
tell them to bugger off.

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.792
Rooney, don't have all day
to bark at you,

00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:50.125
so I'm gonna make this
short and sweet.

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:51.625
Practically perfect.
I love it.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:54.292
I want my daughter
out in front of the school

00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:57.458
in ten minutes by herself.
I don't want anybody--

00:04:57.542 --> 00:04:58.375
What?

00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:00.292
Too suspicious,
he'll think something's up.

00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:01.250
-Cover it.
-You.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:03.833
-Talk! Talk!
-You! Come on!

00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:04.917
3-0-6.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.208
-Talk! No!
-Please.

00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:10.125
-Rooney! Rooney!
-Yes, sir, yes?

00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:11.750
I don't care,
now pay attention.

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:12.792
I changed my mind.

00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:15.458
I want you
out in front of the school,

00:05:15.542 --> 00:05:17.625
I'd like to have a few words
with you, by God!

00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:20.958
On second thought,

00:05:21.042 --> 00:05:22.542
don't have time
to talk right now.

00:05:22.625 --> 00:05:24.375
We'll get together soon
and have lunch.

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:28.167
The rules of The Sneak
are simple and thus

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.167
Follow them close,
you could steal a crust

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.208
-Or a crumpet rind
-Or a pinch of pie

00:05:32.292 --> 00:05:34.708
Or the grease from the tip
of a soggy French fry

00:05:35.708 --> 00:05:37.708
Crumbs and crusts
and stale bread

00:05:37.792 --> 00:05:39.833
Soggy flakes and bin dregs

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:44.583
Any old leftovers
We'll sneak home with us

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:47.208
First find a secret entrance

00:05:47.292 --> 00:05:49.125
Keep your eyes open wide

00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:50.208
-For a hole
-Or a crack

00:05:50.292 --> 00:05:51.458
Or a window with a gap

00:05:51.542 --> 00:05:53.458
Just enough
to squeeze inside

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.750
Once we're in
we creep around

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:00.000
Tiptoe past without a sound

00:06:00.083 --> 00:06:02.125
Keep to the shadows
don't get heard

00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:04.417
Whisper every single word

00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:08.792
Walk as we show you to.

00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:10.708
Eyes up, up, up. Up!

00:06:11.292 --> 00:06:13.667
Speak as we tell you to.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.208
What whim
led White Witney to whittle?

00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:21.417
What whim
led White Witney to whittle?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.417
Act, think,
be as we tell you,

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.042
and you'll become
acceptable wives

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:30.333
and responsible mothers.

00:06:35.333 --> 00:06:37.875
Follow the path
of so many girls

00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:40.333
who once stood
where you do now.

00:06:40.417 --> 00:06:42.208
And just
as we moulded them...

00:06:45.875 --> 00:06:48.750
so shall we you.

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:52.292
We don't work together
in the real world, Bo.

00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:54.500
You're supposed to be
with someone like Bekah.

00:06:55.625 --> 00:06:57.167
What are you talking about?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.625
God. I'm talking about this!

00:07:01.917 --> 00:07:03.542
How are you missing this?

00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:04.542
Do you not know

00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:06.333
what it would feel like
to be with me?

00:07:06.417 --> 00:07:08.917
Never took you for the type
that cares what people think

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.208
I can't, Bo.

00:07:10.792 --> 00:07:12.292
That might
make me a coward, but--

00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:13.208
It does!

00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:17.083
Willowdean Dixon...

00:07:18.875 --> 00:07:20.042
I think you're beautiful.

00:07:22.083 --> 00:07:24.167
To hell with anyone else

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.042
who's ever made you feel
less than that.

00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:33.167
My name is Gabriela Diaz.

00:07:34.042 --> 00:07:35.167
You killed my father.

00:07:35.792 --> 00:07:36.917
Prepare to die!

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:39.667
Gilbert.

00:07:42.458 --> 00:07:44.000
Oh, hi, Gilbert.

00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:52.792
It's just a collar.

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:06.375
Come on!

00:08:16.708 --> 00:08:17.542
Gilbert!

